nted matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." 13194139535617 17592186045443 true] [17592186523113 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523092 13194139535617 17592186045443 true] [17592186523113 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523124 13194139535617 17592186045443 true] [17592186523113 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535617 17592186045443 true] [17592186523113 1077 "III" 13194139535617 17592186045443 true] [17592186523113 1078 #edb/ref 17592186523124 13194139535617 17592186045443 true] [17592186523113 1079 #uuid "2c4297dc-f995-5396-8e9e-d024c65ce177" 13194139535617 17592186045443 true] [17592186523114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523121 13194139535617 17592186045443 true] [17592186523114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523188 13194139535617 17592186045443 true] [17592186523114 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408166 13194139535617 17592186045443 true] [17592186523114 1077 "I" 13194139535617 17592186045443 true] [17592186523114 1078 #edb/ref 17592186523121 13194139535617 17592186045443 true] [17592186523114 1079 #uuid "2ddd758a-c236-567f-9e01-d88d008f82a6" 13194139535617 17592186045443 true] [17592186523115 1075 #edb